Z||000006||frontal lobe||10-11-2001||09:22 PM||||When I was in medical school, we always had cadaver lab Friday mornings, and then picked up our notes for the week right after.  The several hundred pages of notes were not collated, but each page in a stack to be picked up--spread across tables in 2 large rooms.  When you try to pick up one sheet of paper off a stack hundreds of times, the sheets often stick together so the natural reflex is to wet your fingers with your tongue so you can get just one sheet.<P>Yuk.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tigger||10-11-2001||10:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroGT 914:<BR><B>Hey Mach10, I feel for ya - Engineering isn't much better...  The typical week consists of homework problems that take about 1-2 hours and at least 3 pages each and you're lucky to get the right answer when you're done   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I know exactly how you feel.  Here's one problem I had last week.<P>A spherical interplanetary probe of 0.5m diameter contains electronics that dissipate 150W.  If the probe surface has an emissitivity of 0.8 and (get this) the probe does not recieve radiation from other surfaces, as, for example, from the sun, what is its surface temperature? <P>Well, I got Ts = 254.73K<P>*sigh*  This should come in handy someday...  makes for great conversation while on dates.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||bHooper||10-11-2001||10:21 PM||||Hey Phil, since your the resident taxidermist... do you think I could get you to stuff a squirrel for me?  I've always wanted a stuffed squirrel, reared back on his hind legs, for the mantle.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>hoop<P>btw, i majored in Alternative Energies (Passive solar technologies).  they dont come much more useless than that!||||reg||1
