Z||000026||Nashco||10-13-2001||05:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroGT 914:<BR><B>Hey Mach10, I feel for ya - Engineering isn't much better...  The typical week consists of homework problems that take about 1-2 hours and at least 3 pages each and you're lucky to get the right answer when you're done   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"> <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yup...I'm right there too; studying to be a mechanical engineer (automotive powertrain specialty) in Flint, MI at Kettering University (Formerly GMI).  That's the long way of saying it <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Normally, I'm just an M.E.  I can't stand math and sciences, but I'm pretty good with them, and that's what it takes to get into engineering, so here I am.<P>I'm fortunate enough to have not had to deal with thermo, not taking any fields classes, and haven't gotten into any really hard classes; calc II and phys II were the hardest so far, but calc III was easy...go figure!  I wish I just had all the hard classes out of the way so I could take the fun ones!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<P>||||reg||1
